# Mini stack register based VM meant to work with Builtin-BareMetal profile for FP-RISC
# The design:
# r0-r7: general purpose registers
# r8: stack pointer
# r9: PC
# r10: flags -- meant to be reserved right now

# Meant to be a full language and DSL within FP-RISC.
# So it has its own parser and compiles to Stax Bytecode
# Which runs on the Stax VM.

# The memory:
# The stack is a fixed size of N bytes parameterized by the entry point
# There is no routines, and no heap. The stack is the only memory available to the program.
